      "local_deviation": "A Local implementation may manage local agent teammates; human invitation and organization membership actions must remain structurally unavailable when no cloud membership authority exists.",
      "judgment_rationale": "The Web Team page combines project human membership with project-scoped agent teammates. Its UserManager lists, updates and removes project members, but the visible invitation form sends POST /tenants/{tenant_id}/invitations through invitationService rather than adding a project member. Invitation therefore requires tenant-admin authority, while role changes and removal retain project-admin authority. At bb487b613, production Desktop route and workbench consumers resolve `service:desktop-renderer.project-team-authority@1.0.0` through project-scoped generation leases. Each load freezes config, scope and signal before admission; keeps workspace-context, current-user, member and agent reads within one pinned generation; validates exact service, authority, scope and result shapes; rejects duplicate member or agent IDs; revokes escaped authorities after release; and preserves a primary operation failure over disposer failure. Cloud transport remains vault-bound through desktopApiFetch and is explicitly degraded to view, list-members and list-agent-teammates because the Desktop surface exposes no invitation, role, removal or start-chat control. Local has no sidecar Team authority and fails closed before transport with local_project_team_authority_unavailable and no actions. These facts establish renderer authority wiring only and do not constitute native Electron QA, a globally-ready publication, ACK or release readiness, or V1 retirement."
    },
